From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 13:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: scmi: don't skip thermal-zone registration when
 optional sensor config_set is unsupported

CIX Sky1 firmware doesn't implement the optional SCMI sensor
config_set command (Failed to get FC for protocol 13, then
config_set returns -ENOENT for all 20 sensors, confirmed live on
Orion O6N 2026-07-18). config_set is only meant to enable continuous
updates -- an optimization, not a prerequisite for valid readings --
sensors already return correct values without it (verified: 14/20
scmi_sensors hwmon temp*_input entries read real board temperatures
on this platform).

But the probe loop `continue`s past scmi_thermal_sensor_register()
whenever config_set fails, which on this firmware means it fires for
every single sensor. Net effect: none of CPU_B0/B1/M0/M1, GPU_top/
btm/AVE, NPU, VPU, DDR_top/btm, SOC_BRC/TRC, CI ever get a kernel
thermal zone / cooling-device binding -- confirmed live: only 5
generic acpitz zones exist, zero scmi-backed ones. No automatic
throttling governance on any SoC-internal sensor, only whatever the
coarse ACPI thermal zones cover.

Fix: treat a failed config_set as informational (dev_dbg, this
firmware just doesn't support the optional enable), not fatal to
this sensor's probe -- fall through to attempt thermal-zone
registration regardless, same as before for any sensor whose
config_set does succeed.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c b/drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c
@@ -341,11 +341,10 @@ static int scmi_hwmon_probe(struct scmi_device *sdev)
 		if (!sensor)
 			continue;

 		ret = sensor_ops->config_set(ph, i, sensor_config);
-		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(dev, "Error enabling sensor %s. err=%d\n",
-				sensor->name, ret);
-			continue;
-		}
+		if (ret)
+			dev_dbg(dev,
+				"Sensor %s: optional config_set unsupported by firmware, err=%d (continuing without it)\n",
+				sensor->name, ret);

 		/*
 		 * Warn on any misconfiguration related to thermal zones but
--
2.51.0
